# GitHub push — every ship (Builder)

After **every** version bump + successful `_ship_check.ps1`:

1. Run `_git_ship.ps1` with the new version:
   ```powershell
   powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "_git_ship.ps1" -Version X.Y.Z
   ```
2. **First time only** (no `origin`): run `_push_to_github.ps1` to create/link the repo, then `_git_ship.ps1` again.

## What it does

- `git add -A` (respects `.gitignore` — no zips, no game logs, no `.tools/`)
- Commit: `ship vX.Y.Z: <modinfo description>`
- `git push origin main`
- Annotated tag `vX.Y.Z` + `git push origin vX.Y.Z` (force-update tag if same version re-shipped)

## Rollback

```powershell
git checkout v1.1.5
# or: git revert <commit>
```

## Ship checklist (full tail)

1. Bump version + implement fixes
2. `_ship_check.ps1` → fluffy zip
3. `_wipe_game_logs.ps1 -Version X.Y.Z`
4. **`_git_ship.ps1 -Version X.Y.Z`** ← required every ship
5. SHIP HANDOFF must include `GITHUB: main @ <hash> tag=vX.Y.Z` or `GITHUB: FAIL — <reason>`

## Hard ban

- Do not call a build "shipped" in SHIP HANDOFF if GitHub push was skipped without stating why
- Do not commit game-folder paths, fluffy zips, or secrets

## Repo

- Workspace: `QuestTracker-Modded/`
- Remote name: `origin`, branch: `main`
- Tags: `v` + `MOD_VERSION` (e.g. `v1.1.6`)
